<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  WreckedMachines_HideDonorSmelter.xml          mandrake.rm.wreckedmachines

  WRECKEDMACHINES_VFE_SMELTER_REMOVAL_1. Owner ruling 2026-09-16, verbatim:
  "remove the VFE factory, not the manual one." About.xml called the donor's
  Automated Smelter staying buildable alongside our three restoration tiers
  "a testing arrangement, not a finished one" — this file finishes it.

  WHICH SMELTER, EXACTLY
  =======================
  There are two smelters in play and only one is in scope:

    * VFEFactory_AutomatedSmelter — the donor's fully-automated smelter
      (Buildings_Factories.xml, packageId VanillaExpanded.VFEFactory,
      workshop 3686924415, /1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Buildings/Buildings_
      Factories.xml:185). Auto-pulls from hoppers, no player attention once
      running. THIS is "the VFE factory" the ruling names — it is exactly
      what our RM_WM_AutomatedSmelter_Wrecked/Kludged/Repaired ladder exists
      to replace narratively, and it is the def our own def file's header
      already documents as "a known, accepted cost of the testing phase,
      NOT acceptable at ship."

    * ElectricSmelter — VANILLA's own hand-run smelter (queue a "Smelt
      weapon"/"Smelt apparel" bill, work it like any other bench). This is
      "the manual one" the ruling protects. It is not part of VFE-Factory,
      it is not touched by anything in this mod, and this file does not
      reference it at all — named here only so nobody "fixes" it later
      by mistake.

  WHY designationCategory AND NOT DELETING THE DEF
  ==================================================
  Same reasoning as the proven precedent in this stack
  (RSW_Armoury/Patches/Warcasket_BuildPathCut.xml, which removed the
  droid-factory-class building the same way): our own Kludged and Repaired
  tiers reference the donor's ProcessDefs directly (VFEFactory_
  SmeltMetalFromSlag, _SmeltMetalFromMechSlag, _SmeltWeapon —
  Buildings_WreckedMachines_AutomatedSmelter.xml). Deleting
  VFEFactory_AutomatedSmelter itself, or its recipes, would either break
  those references or require duplicating the recipes into our own defs for
  no reason. Clearing <designationCategory> removes it from the Architect
  menu — the only place a player can newly acquire one — while leaving the
  ThingDef, its comps and its processes completely intact for anything that
  still reads them (including, if the donor mod ever spawns one via a quest
  or map-gen, an already-placed instance).

  Wrapped in PatchOperationFindMod so this is a silent no-op if VFE-Factory
  is ever removed (impossible today — About.xml lists it as a hard
  modDependency — but free insurance). PatchOperationConditional guards the
  cut itself so a VFE-Factory update that restructures the def makes this
  fall silent rather than error.

  VERIFY AFTER THE NEXT LOAD
  ===========================
    * Architect > Factories: NO "automated smelter" (the donor's). Our own
      three RM_WM_AutomatedSmelter_* tiers are unaffected — this patch only
      strips <designationCategory> from VFEFactory_AutomatedSmelter by
      defName, and our tiers carry the SAME category
      (VFEFactory_Factories, per Buildings_WreckedMachines_
      AutomatedSmelter.xml) on their own separate ThingDefs, so the category
      itself stays populated and visible.
    * Architect > Production: vanilla's "electric smelter" is present and
      unchanged.
    * grep Player.log for "Could not resolve cross-reference" — no new hits
      naming VFEFactory_AutomatedSmelter or its processes; our own tiers
      still resolve their <li>VFEFactory_Smelt...</li> process references.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Vanilla Furniture Expanded - Factory</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="VFEFactory_AutomatedSmelter"]/designationCategory</xpath>
      <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
        <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="VFEFactory_AutomatedSmelter"]/designationCategory</xpath>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
